 "body": "Second adversarial review round (5 parallel auditors on Java/C#/Go/TS/Python\nresolution, the five ops, and astkit) found a batch of real correctness bugs\nof the same \"family/site silently dropped\" class. All fixed with regression\ntests; all 13 corpus ceilings re-verified identical to baseline (these paths\nweren't exercised by the measured tasks \u2014 the paper numbers were correct, now\nproven by fixing the bugs and re-measuring rather than asserting it).\n\nGo:\n- buildContains + missing-impl closure now include KindType: a method on a\n  named non-struct type (`type Status int`) \u2014 Go's idiomatic non-struct\n  receiver \u2014 was completely invisible to change-impact and missing-impl.\n- buildExtendsImplements handles interface-embeds-interface (was struct-only);\n  goEmbeddedTypes regex now matches cross-package `pkg.Type` embeds.\n\nchange-impact:\n- The empty-set gate ran before contract synthesis, so an interface method\n  with zero current implementors threw a false \"declares no method\" \u2014 the most\n  basic \"what breaks if I change this\" query. Synthesis now runs first.\n\nrename-plan / untested-surface:\n- Sites() now unions Supers (methods), so a rename seeded on an implementation\n  no longer drops ",
